<title>FRANCE: French business leaders see jobs fall in Q4 1996.</title>
<headline>French business leaders see jobs fall in Q4 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French business leaders expect to see a fairly significant fall in workers in industry in the fourth quarter of 1996, according to a quarterly survey by national statistics institute INSEE.</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following data, seasonally adjusted unless stated:</p>
<p>					   Oct    July   Apr    Oct 95</p>
<p>Past trend</p>
<p> Total industry			-22    -18     -8     -7</p>
<p> Manufacturing industry (unadj)  -22    -12    -10     -7</p>
<p>Future trend</p>
<p> Total industry (unadj)	    -28    -20    -12    -18</p>
<p> Manufacturing industry (unadj)  -29    -20    -12    -19</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
</text>
